% M2-L8 control, scene 2 of 2: THE CHANGED VARIANT.
%
% The base refutation plus a spectator p that is NOT fixed: width 2 against x and y's
% width 4, so first-fail branches on it FIRST and the whole refutation moves one level
% down. Measured 2026-09-18, against the base:
%
%     nodes 7 -> 8, decisions 3 -> 4, maxdepth 3 -> 4, skipped 0 -> 1
%     .pbp 1275 -> 1315 B, 21 -> 25 level markers
%
% Note that the PROOF columns move here too, and by a similar amount to scene 1. That
% is deliberate: a classifier that looked only at proof size would call these two rows
% the same kind of event. The tree columns are what tell them apart, and `-c` requires
% the verdict `CHANGED` here -- meaning the other columns are not a like-for-like
% comparison on this row and must not be quoted as one.
%
% `skipped` moving 0 -> 1 is the second half of why M1-T36's nodes-only rule is not
% enough for a learning benchmark: with backjumping in the solver, a tree can move
% while its node count does not.
var 0..1: p :: output_var;
var 0..3: x :: output_var;
var 0..3: y :: output_var;
constraint int_ne(x, y);
constraint int_eq(x, y);
solve satisfy;
